BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Web Design for Entrepreneurs (Newcomer Stream)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T193000
UID:69d95a8ec1cf6f9a75847e25@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this\n8-week course\n\, learn how to build a strong web pre
 sence for your business in Toronto\, whether you’re launching something 
 new or already running one. Explore how to create a website using WordPres
 s and understand why it remains a powerful tool\, even in the age of AI we
 bsite builders. While AI can help you get started quickly\, WordPress giv
 es you full control over your content\, updates\, and long-term growth. By
  the end\, you’ll feel more confident managing your own website\, saving
  costs while strengthening your marketing at the same time.\nParticipants 
 should plan to attend all 8 of the following d\nates:\nMay 6\, May 13\,\n
 May 20\nJune 3\, June 17\, June 24\nJuly 8\, July 15\nRegistration is requ
 ired for the full series\n. This program is hosted by the Business\, Scien
 ce and Technology department. Please visit the 4th floor service desk or c
 all (416) 395-5613 for more information.\nThis program is part of the\n"Bu
 ilding your own Website for Small Business" Program Series (Newcomer strea
 m)\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, e-Learning Lab\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d95a8ec1cf6f9a75847e25
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Night Sparrow: Celebrating Unsung Jewish Women Erased From His
 tory
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T153000
UID:69ab65c74a9fd98b7f82a5a5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The first Jewish female snipers in history fought against the 
 'fascist Nazis' in WWII\, yet their astonishing stories are visually unkno
 wn. Forbidden to speak about their achievements after the war\, these wome
 n were erased by the country they fought to protect.\nDiscover how these i
 ndomitable women changed history in this presentation by author Shelly San
 ders\, whose novel\nThe Night Sparrow\nwas inspired by their recently tran
 slated diaries\, photos\, and frontline stories.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Located in Room B on the third floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ab65c74a9fd98b7f82a5a5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monthly Movie Screening: Marmalade
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T200000
UID:69961fbcb0595799c09dc5bf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This month's feature:\nMarmalade\nEnjoy a night at the movies!
  Join us for a free movie on the big screen in our accessible theatre.\nDe
 scription: MARMALADE is an edge-of-the-seat crime-tinged romance tale. Re
 cently incarcerated Baron struck up a friendship with cellmate Otis\, a ma
 n with a well-versed history of prison breaks. As the pair hatch an escape
  plan together\, Baron recalls the story of how he met Marmalade\, the lov
 e of his life\, and their "Bonnie and Clyde" style scheme to rob a bank in
  order to care for his sick mother and give the couple the life they have 
 always dreamed of.\nThis film is rated 14A. 99 minutes. Start time is 6:00
  pm. Drop in. All are welcome!
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Theatre (downstairs)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69961fbcb0595799c09dc5bf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
