SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T200000
UID:697127ac4a9fd98b7f78e26f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the\ninformation session\non\nF
 riday\, April 24\, 2026.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Friday\,\nonce a we
 ek for 8 weeks\, May 1 - June 19\, 2026\, 5:00-8:00pm\n. Registration clo
 ses after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSn
 acks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists 
 will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\
 nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is sol
 ely responsible for the protection of \npersonal information collected thr
 ough the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, 2nd floor\, end of hallway
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697127ac4a9fd98b7f78e26f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Family Ties by Rona Fleising
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260402T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T235959
UID:69b823748d5e2d093365965e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of April\, the works of artist Rona Fleis
 ing are on display at the Yorkville Branch in an exhibit titled Family Ti
 es.\nRona is a folk artist crafting whimsical portraits from retired men's
  ties\, vintage buttons\, and reclaimed notions. She began her studies in 
 Montreal at university followed by studio work in NYC. In Calgary\, she w
 as an education officer at the Glenbow Museum\, tour guide for Arts & Cult
 ure\, freelance art consultant\, and advisor to the mayor's office on publ
 ic art. Now she lives in Toronto where she is pursuing her goal of an exh
 ibition in her golden years.\n"Family Ties refers to the bonds between fam
 ily members which can include emotional connections and practical support.
  Rona breathes new life and purpose into her collection of ties\, buttons
 \, and notions donated by family and friends. Graphic design training insp
 ires her to integrate the colours and patterns of each tie with decorativ
 e elements to develop unique persona. She approaches art as serious fun\, 
 incorporating hand-sewing with visual literacy and a measure of wit."\nTh
 is exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Public L
 ibrary provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations
  across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural inter
 ests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during
 \nYorkville\nbranch open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Art
 ist: Rona Fleising\; Eilish
LOCATION:Yorkville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b823748d5e2d093365965e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Master Your Taxes:  A Guide to Keeping the CRA Happy for Entrepren
 eurs\, Freelancers\, and Self-employed Canadians
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260505T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260505T193000
UID:69cdb092f29b90618efd229c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:As shifts in the economy and available technologies change the
  reality of work\, more and more Canadians are dipping into the world of s
 elf-employment\, consulting and freelancing. Starting a new endeavor can b
 e thrilling\, but it comes with challenges\, as well. One of those is the 
 new complexity of the unique tax issues that come with running a business.
 \nJoin us for an entertaining and information-packed presentation by Sunn
 y Widerman about the financial and tax aspects of running your own busine
 ss.\nNote: This is\nnot\na tax clinic.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, 1st Fl
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cdb092f29b90618efd229c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
