BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Entrepreneur Insights Panel: Real Stories\, Real Lessons
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T200000
UID:69b831192b552e8e21b32b8c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Lily Akagbosu\, Newcomer Entrepreneur in Residence\nBehind eve
 ry successful business is a journey filled with experimentation\, learning
 \, and perseverance. Hearing directly from entrepreneurs who have navigate
 d that journey can offer valuable perspective and inspiration.\nIn this in
 teractive panel session\, guest entrepreneurs will share honest insights f
 rom their experiences building and growing their businesses. Participants 
 will hear about early challenges\, important decisions\, and lessons learn
 ed along the way. The session will include a moderated discussion followed
  by audience questions\, giving attendees the opportunity to gain practica
 l advice and real-world insights from founders who have been through the e
 ntrepreneurial process.\nFood and non-alcoholic refreshments will be provi
 ded. While we strive to offer allergy-aware options for common dietary nee
 ds\, food is prepared and served in shared facilities and we cannot guaran
 tee an allergen-free environment.\nRegistration is required.\nNewcomer Ent
 repreneur in Residence:\nLily Akagbosu is a Product Manager and entreprene
 ur with a Master’s degree in Digital Product Management from Queen’s U
 niversity. She has shaped and delivered products at organizations includin
 g IBM\, Shopify\, and the Bank of Montreal. Beyond her product work\, she 
 has built hands-on business experience through startup ventures\, commerce
 \, and consulting. Over the years\, Lily has actively engaged in Canada’
 s entrepreneurship ecosystem through the University of Toronto’s Black F
 ounders Network\, Venture for Canada\, ventureLAB\, and NEXT Canada. She s
 upports entrepreneurs and aspiring business owners from idea through launc
 h and growth\, and delivers talks on leadership and innovation.\nPanelists
 :\nNeda Ghazi\, PhD\nFounder of Comfable\nDr. Neda Ghazi is an entrepreneu
 r and digital product leader with a track record of building and scaling t
 echnology products used by millions worldwide. She has been recognized as 
 one of Canada’s Top 50 Inspiring Women in Tech. She is the founder of Co
 mfable\, a digital product studio that works with startups and organizatio
 ns to design and build impactful digital solutions\, and the founder of Me
 ex\, a platform focused on enabling more intentional professional connecti
 ons. Her work sits at the intersection of AI\, product strategy\, and grow
 th\, with a focus on how technology can create more meaningful and accessi
 ble human experiences. Products she has led\, including Sun Index and UV W
 eather\, have been featured by Google and Apple. Beyond her work in tech\,
  Neda supports the startup ecosystem as an advisor and contributes to nonp
 rofit initiatives focused on human rights.\nFolarin Odunayo\nFounder\, TAK
 E3 MEDIA | Account Manager\, SESAMm\nFolarin is an Account Manager by day 
 and a builder by nature. With a career spanning financial services at Weal
 thsimple and CIBC\, merchant success at Shopify\, and now AI-driven data a
 nalytics at SESAMm\, he has spent over a decade at the intersection of str
 ategy\, relationships\, and growth. Outside the 9–5\, Folarin is the fou
 nder of TAKE3 MEDIA\, a business management practice helping musicians nav
 igate the financial and strategic side of their careers. Its production ar
 m has launched live series including Tiny's Session and I Know Thi$ One\, 
 which have carved out a distinct place in Toronto's creative community. Fr
 om digital magazines to podcasts to international tours\, each chapter of 
 his journey has been a lesson in turning ideas into something that lasts.\
 nIndrani Ray\nFounder & Chief Strategist\, Maia Marketing\nIndrani is an a
 ward-winning marketing leader with 25 years of experience driving growth f
 or global B2B tech companies\, including UKG\, PointClickCare\, and Achiev
 ers. She has led marketing through mergers and acquisitions\, new market e
 ntries\, and major rebranding initiatives across the US and Canada\, and h
 as built joint programs with organizations including Anthropic\, Google\, 
 and Workday. Her areas of deep expertise span brand strategy\, demand gene
 ration\, PR\, analyst relations\, and go-to-market execution. Indrani hold
 s an M.A. from Purdue University.\nThis program is part of Toronto Public 
 Library’s\nNewcomer Entrepreneur in Residence\nprogram series and\nNewco
 mer Entrepreneurship Initiative\n\, designed to support newcomers as they 
 explore entrepreneurship and build practical small business skills. Partic
 ipants will learn about key topics for starting and growing a business in 
 Canada\, with guidance from an experienced entrepreneur in residence. For 
 more information and a full list of programs\, visit\ntpl.ca/eir\n.\nInfor
 mation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collec
 ted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, section
 s 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event a
 nd program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the
  library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\n
 answerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
 .
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Room 204
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b831192b552e8e21b32b8c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
