DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T200000
UID:69e28789b1165a41a65fe3dc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Mottled Duskywing butterfly\, found only in a handful of h
 abitats in Ontario\, is vanishing at an alarming rate. Witness the inspiri
 ng efforts of a dedicated recovery team as they work tirelessly to bring t
 his species back to its former range.\nJoin us for a screening of\nButterf
 lies on the Brink\n: The Story of the Mottled Duskywing\n\, a gripping doc
 umentary about a rare butterfly species' fight for survival on the edge of
  extinction.\nThe film is approximately 47 minutes\, followed by a Q&A pan
 el with\nMiles Finlayson\n\, the director of Butterflies On The Brink with
  special guests\,\nAdrienne Brewster\n\, Executive Director of Cambridge 
 Butterfly Conservatory.\nFree. Registration required. Doors open at 6:15 p
 m. At 6:30 pm\, seating becomes first-come\, first-served until capacity i
 s reached.\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram ser
 ies\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​\n
 Questions? Please contact North York Central Library - Business\, Science 
 & Technology Department.\nInformation Collection Notice: The personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge 
 Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium (2nd floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e28789b1165a41a65fe3dc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
