SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC): Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260428T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260428T200000
UID:69b1b3f71e64afd01e6164a7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nA Writers Collective of Canada (WCC) workshop is unlike any other
 . We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\, l
 isten deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into yo
 ur story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\, a
 nd respect. (wcc-cec.org)\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. 
 Materials are provided.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b1b3f71e64afd01e6164a7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Restaurant Kid: A Memoir of Family and Belonging
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T200000
UID:69b2ee806583d22e3c0ec318@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Rachel Phan is a Chinese-Vietnamese Canadian writer whose debu
 t memoir\nRestaurant Kid\nexplores the complexities of growing up as the d
 aughter of refugees who fled the Vietnam War and rebuilt their lives throu
 gh a small-town restaurant in Canada. Through personal stories rooted in r
 esilience\, sacrifice\, and belonging\, Rachel sheds light on the impact o
 f colonialism\, intergenerational trauma\, and the emotional weight of cul
 tural and societal expectations.\nA Q&A and book signing will follow the p
 resentation.\nNo registration required.
LOCATION:Yorkville\, Centre of library
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b2ee806583d22e3c0ec318
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
