BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google AI Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T200000
UID:69dc55718ddc1caf5f1c8317@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about artificial intelligence (AI)? Let
 's learn the basics of AI in a welcoming space.\nWe will meet online via Z
 oom on\nMay 7- May 28\, 2026 from 6-8pm.\nAI Essentials Learning Circles a
 re study groups guided by staff for people who want to take the Google AI 
 Essentials online course together in a welcoming space. Learners meet week
 ly and work together through the course materials. Participants are expect
 ed to commit to the duration of the course and attend all learning circle 
 sessions.\nGoogle AI Essentials is designed to help people across roles an
 d industries get essential AI skills to boost their productivity. Zero exp
 erience is required.\nAt each session\, you'll discuss the content of the 
 course\, have time to catch up on the course work\, and learn about relate
 d library resources.\nGoogle AI Essentials consists of 5 sections and take
 s approximately 10 hours to complete:\nIntroduction to AI - Learn about fo
 undational concepts such as machine learning and generative AI.\nMaximize 
 productivity with AI tools - Learn how to use generative AI tools to incre
 ase productivity in completing work tasks.\nDiscover the art of prompting 
 - Learn how to write effective prompts to get better outputs using AI tool
 s.\nUse AI responsibly - Learn how to lessen harmful biases and inaccuraci
 es. Recognize the security risks of using AI in the workplace.\nStay Ahead
  of the AI Curve - Learn how to stay up-to-date with the latest AI news.\n
 Access to the course and certification are provided at no cost to individu
 als who participate in the learning circle.\nLearners who complete the cou
 rse will be able to:\nearn a certificate to be shared on LinkedIn and soci
 al media profiles\ndownload a certificate of completion\nThe registration 
 process is a two-step procedure. First\, participants must complete their 
 registration through this page. After this step\, library staff will follo
 w up to request additional information in order to complete the registrati
 on.\nParticipants must have a valid Toronto Public Library card to registe
 r.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dc55718ddc1caf5f1c8317
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
