BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author’s Talk-Will Power
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T200000
UID:69dfdec5defec6489cbe033d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Author\, Susan Goldenberg\, shares stories from her book\,\nWi
 ll Power\n\, about recent and past wills of famous and "ordinary" people f
 rom across Canada. Unusually unique\, the first book on this topic contain
 s landmark cases of gender discrimination and cautionary tales of family c
 onflicts.  There's the eccentric will that left a mansion and its grounds 
 to a parrot. Developers could do nothing until it died -- and parrots have
  long lives. There is the one-page will fought over for two decades by thr
 ee generations. These stories and many more\, will amuse\, entertain\, sho
 ck and inform.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, 1st floor\, Beeton Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dfdec5defec6489cbe033d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
