BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Amazing Evening with Lloyd Penney
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T193000
UID:69cd43e41e64afd01e661b49@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an interview with local editor\, proofreader and s
 cience fiction fan Lloyd Penney. Lloyd is the current editor-in-chief of A
 mazing Stories Magazine\, the first science fiction-only magazine. We will
  discuss the editing process\, the 100-year legacy of Amazing\, and the jo
 ys of science fiction. A Q&A and booksale will follow the talk.\nHosted by
  the\nMerril Collection of Science Fiction\, Speculation & Fantasy\n. Thi
 s event is a tie-in to our current exhibit\,\nAmazing! Fantastic! Astoundi
 ng! Science Fiction and the Pulp Magazines\n.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Merril Collection Reading Room\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cd43e41e64afd01e661b49
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Northern District Book Club—Afternoons
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T150000
UID:6974edc676261f280066713c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a friendly\, spirited discussion of a different bo
 ok on the second Wednesday of each month. We read an eclectic mix of mostl
 y contemporary fiction.\nThere is also an evening session to discuss the s
 ame book on the third Wednesday of each month at 7:00 p.m.  You are welc
 ome at either or both!\nApril 8\, 2026:\nThe Mountains Sing\nby Phan Qu
 ế Mai Nguyễn\nMay 13\, 2026:\nSea of Tranquility\nby Emily St. John M
 andel [\nNote:\nthis is a change.]\nJune 10\, 2026:\nPrairie Edge\nby Cono
 r Kerr\nJuly 8\, 2026:\nLiberation Day\nby George Saunders\nSeptember 9\, 
 2026:\nOrbital\nby Samantha Harvey\nOctober 14\, 2026:\nMaybe You Should T
 alk to Someone\nby Lori Gottlieb\nNovember 11\, 2026:\nStone Yard Devotion
 al\nby Charlotte Wood\nDecember 9\, 2026:\nThe Laundryman's Boy\nby Edward
  Y. C. Lee
LOCATION:Northern District\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6974edc676261f280066713c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
