DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260504T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260504T200000
UID:69a0af074a9fd98b7f80c90f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Authors Genevieve Graham\, Kate Hilton and Heather Marshall di
 scuss their new historical fictions novels.\nTaking us from a turn-of-the-
 century archaeological dig to a 1920s hotel and a midcentury newsroom\, be
 stselling writers Graham (\nThe Chambermaid's Key\n)\, Hilton (\nCity of t
 he Muse\n) and Marshall (\nLiberty Street\n) share three riveting new hist
 orical fiction stories brimming with mystery and suspense.\nThe authors sp
 eak with arts and life reporter Aparita Bhandari about their new books\, t
 he art of writing about a bygone era and the eternal appeal of travelling 
 back in time by book.\nQ&A and book signing to follow. Books available for
  purchase.\nAbout this event’s guests:\nGenevieve Graham\nKate Hilton\nH
 eather Marshall\nAparita Bhandari\nRead more:\nChambermaid's Key : A Novel
 \nCity of the Muse\nLiberty Street\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nConc
 ourse Event Space\, North York Central Library (5120 Yonge St)\nTime:\nDoo
 rs open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration require
 d.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell these events to ensure that the greatest n
 umber of people have an opportunity to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 6:
 45pm or until capacity is reached. Seating first come\, first served.\n***
 \nThis event is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where we host loca
 l and international authors\, artists and thinkers in conversation about t
 heir new books and big ideas.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
