BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Richard III: Discovered and Uncovered
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260506T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260506T200000
UID:69b47146ad384e40edb42b46@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In 2012\, an archaeological dig found the remains of a long lo
 st medieval king. Sheilah O’Connor of the Richard III Society explains w
 hy a woman risked ridicule in her quest to find this controversial monarch
 . And then\, how mitochondria DNA\, X-Rays and a Canadian connection tell 
 a different story about this man.\nSheilah O’Connor is a retired librari
 an and a member of the Canadian Branch of the Richard III Society. She is 
 a semi-regular writer for the Society’s publications. Sheilah has been s
 peaking about Richard III for over 20 years. Audiences have included high 
 school students\, members of various Historical Associations and attendees
  at the Stratford Festival. She was in Leicester during the week that Rich
 ard III was reburied\, and watched the event on a big screen in a square n
 ear the cathedral\nBooks and Media on Richard III\nNon-fiction books\nThe 
 Last Days of Richard III\nThe King's Grave\nThe Princes in the Tower\nRich
 ard III\nFiction books\nThis Son of York\nThe Sunne in Splendour\nThe Daug
 hter of Time\nRequiem of the Rose King\nFilm\nThe Lost King\nThe White Que
 en\nResurrecting Richard III
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Upstairs in room 204
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b47146ad384e40edb42b46
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:L'art de la Fabrication Artisanale : Des Accessoires d'Inspiration
  Africaine en Tissus Wax (The Art of Handcrafting: Afro-Inspired Accessori
 es with Wax Fabrics)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260428T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260428T153000
UID:69bbf86e2866a5b488431362@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Découvrez le riche patrimoine culturel de l'Afrique à traver
 s l'exploration des tissus wax. Plongez-vous dans l'histoire et la symboli
 que de ces tissus\, véritables objets d'art ou accessoires uniques qui al
 lient créativité\, savoir-faire et découverte culturelle. Cette présen
 tation interactive consacrée aux tissus wax aborde leurs origines histori
 ques et leur symbolique\, leur processus de fabrication ainsi que leur imp
 ortance culturelle. Des échantillons seront mis à disposition pour vous 
 permettre de comparer les tissus wax artisanaux et industriels.\nAccessibi
 lité:\nLe sous-titrage en direct ou automatique\, l’interprétation en 
 langue des signes\, les services d’intervenant\, ou les services d’acc
 ompagnement sont disponibles sur demande. Veuillez soumettre votre demand
 e au moins deux semaines à l’avance à : tpl.ca/accessibility-events\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Room 224
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bbf86e2866a5b488431362
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
