BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Journalism Series with David Silverberg: What do editors want from
  freelance journalists? (panel discussion)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T193000
UID:69c81fe8b48451fc3c0bd8f7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This panel discussion is presented by the North York Central 
 Library's 2026 Writer in Residence David Silverberg\, whose focus is on Jo
 urnalism.\nLearn from editors who have witnessed it all. Joining David on 
 a panel discussion to share their insight on ideas they’d like to see fr
 om freelance journalists\, Toronto-based editors Navneet Alang (opinions 
 editor\, The Toronto Star) and Judith Pereira (arts editor\, The Globe & 
 Mail) will reveal their favourite pitches and discuss the types of articl
 es they publish. The panel will also discuss pay rates\, developing relati
 onships with editors and their top Do’s and Don’ts.\nThis discussion w
 ill be followed by Q&A\nLearn more about TPL's\nWriter in Residence\nprogr
 am\, including upcoming programs and one-on-one consultation sessions.\nIn
 formation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is col
 lected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sect
 ions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for even
 t and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how 
 the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff a
 t\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 
 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101\, 1st floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c81fe8b48451fc3c0bd8f7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists Circle: Crepe Paper Flowers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T160000
UID:69df8e19b6c4ac1fedcc846c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Whether you're a beginner or an experienced artist\, our Artis
 ts Circle program offers a welcoming space to reduce stress\, explore new 
 art techniques\, and connect with fellow art appreciators. Each month\, t
 he library will set out a selection of art books based on a chosen theme.
  We will provide participants with an artistic prompt and materials to cr
 eate their artwork.\nCelebrate the colour and beauty of springtime florals
  with paper flowers that were made to last! Learn how to craft paper ros
 es or peonies to take home or give to a friend. All materials provided\; 
 no experience necessary.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inf
 ormation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the
  Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informatio
 n will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eval
 uation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be di
 rected to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge
  Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69df8e19b6c4ac1fedcc846c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Climate Disinformation: What We Can Do About It
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T131500
UID:69ca8e5e58f0b64d9e7c323c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What do tobacco and fossil fuels have in common\, and why does
  it matter now? How is climate change disinformation being used against Ca
 nadians\, and what can you do to push back? What is Information Sovereignt
 y and Information Integrity\, and why does it matter?\nGet the answers to 
 these questions and more with\nPhil Newell\n\, communications co-chair of 
 the\nClimate Action Against Disinformation coalition\n\, a network of over
  120 organizations around the world\, and learn about the new Global Initi
 ative on Information Integrity on Climate Change.\nThis program is present
 ed as part of\nToronto Climate Week\nand TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogra
 m series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.
 ​\nRegistration:\nThis virtual event is free to join. Once registered\, 
 you’ll receive an email with details on how to join the session.\nThis p
 rogram will take place on\nZoom\nand will be recorded. Registrants will re
 ceive a link to stream the recording after the program. Captions will be a
 vailable.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and participating in a Zoom we
 binar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pers
 onal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library u
 nder the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The in
 formation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery 
 and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information c
 an be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\
 , 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ca8e5e58f0b64d9e7c323c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
